<<~ ahu #/ruling>>

! Recipe Layer Model ~ a scout against the ruling

''Register: Model-Standing.'' A scout read the mount code, the routing cascade, the sync gate, the disk legs, the TW5 fork and the standing canon, whole; the operator ruled; two spirits enacted the model in the mounts, the cascade and the verbs. Every claim below names a file and a line; a claim without one names itself as inference. The #/as-mounted and #/as-routed sections describe the code AS IT STANDS; #/the-blur names what the enactment dissolved and what remains open.

''The operator's ruling, verbatim (quote license):''

> "For each recipe, the 'top bag' gets determined by the kind of raw tiddler. Most go to the 'named wiki bag' (disk projects into the base `/wikis/*` dir for the recipe), BUT `Draft of '...'` and similar tiddlers (#has `draft-of` field, etc) goes to a 'drafts' layer above that (fleet synced just as the wiki's main wiki-bag and the underlying canon-bags). Then there's volatile tiddlers on top of that (most don't sync, I think all here don't, Presence, local-only state, THIS is the per-device layer). Under the `wikis/` layers we have the 'canon bags' from `bags/` (disk ingest/projection-on-move). We need to deeply scout this blur and resolve the code and memes to one 'model architecture'. … Now that we have 'api surface' for memes and not just tiddlers this becomes important to clarify for all incoming files (other files would get ingested as typed tiddlers and round trip to disk with `*.meta` files, etc, so we may need to stub out or find the TW5 api surfaces for those non-tiddler/non-meme workflows)."

The ruling names FOUR strata per recipe — ''canon bags'' ← ''named wiki bag'' ← ''drafts'' ← ''volatile'' — and one routing key: ''the kind of raw tiddler''. The code mounts FIVE per-wiki slots plus a canon and a library floor — `personal` stands as its own layer by a later ruling — and routes drafts by the `draft.of` FIELD, volatile and view-state by kind.

''Five later rulings, verbatim (quote license):''

# Draft doc — "One doc -> fleet IF a PersonaGroup sync-fleet cap available, ELSE this is a 'private device so far'. Pono? Our caps stack 'falls back to the floor' never fails/reds in production."
# `personal` — "Keep as its own layer, as we iterate on what 'needs fleet sync' vs what doesn't after the browser UX stands up."
# `meme get --recipe` — "The stack."
# The daemon wiki — "Approve `working` layers for all wikis (Daemon reads as a wiki with specific caps to the vessel, instead of 'user content')."
# The draft switch — "Approve moving to `draft.of` as the switch".

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/as-mounted>>

!! The layers exactly as three composites mount them today

Three `CompositeStore` instances stand in a running node, and one shape serves the browser. Bottom row first (lowest priority); the top row wins a read. ''`default`'' marks the layer the composite's UNBAGGED writes fall into — `addLayer` re-points `writableStore` at every layer registered with `writable:true` and `defaultWritable !== false` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/composite-store.ts:123`), so the LAST such layer holds the office. ONE law names that layer for every mounter: `slotLayerFlags` / `defaultWritableSlot` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`) — the working slot when its handle stands, else the wiki's canon bag (the floor, never a red); the volatile temp slot NEVER holds the office. Witness: `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/composite-store.test.ts` "the default writable under the recipe layer model".

''Sync class'' reads off the node `sharePolicy`: every Automerge doc full-syncs to an in-process island peer and to a `same-operator` WS peer (the device fleet); a cross-operator peer reaches only the deterministically-federatable planes (`packages/lararium-node/src/self-slot-share.ts:70-95`, `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:434-462`). So ''fleet'' below means //any Automerge doc//; ''device'' means //a `MemoryTiddlerStore` that never enters a Repo//. The browser gate carries the same split (`packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts:370`, `:523`).

!!! A. The wiki ISLAND composite (node and browser — one kernel)

Laid by `expandRecipe` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`) walked bottom-up in `buildIslandRecipe` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-recipe.ts`); slot docs resolve from typed grants in `sovereign-kernel.ts` `slotUrl`. The library bags a recipe RECORD names lay at boot (`recipeFromRecord`, read in `core-caps.ts` `mountCap` and `vessel-residency-wiring.ts` `resolveWikiSpec`), and recipe-watch keeps the same stack live.

| layer (top wins) | store | writable | default | sync class | doc keyed by | disk mirror (node) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wikis/{slug}/temp` | `MemoryTiddlerStore` | yes | ''never'' (`slotLayerFlags`) | device | none — fresh per boot | none |
| `wikis/{slug}/draft` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet when seated · device when not | THE ONE slot-doc resolver (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/slot-doc-resolver.ts`): `daemon/draft-bindings/{fingerprint}` (PersonaGroup × recipe-fingerprint) when the vessel holds a SEAT; else the floor doc `wikis/{slug}/drafts/{did}` in the catalog registry, `face-reach: vessel-only` | none |
| `wikis/{slug}/personal` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet | `daemon/personal-bindings/{fingerprint}` — its own layer by ruling | none |
| `wikis/{slug}/working` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | ''YES'' — the ONE default | fleet | `daemon/working-bindings/{fingerprint}` (the vessel key binds; a seated face composes on top) | `wikis/{slug}/` via the `wikiSlot:"working"` grant (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `vessel-island-pool-core.ts`) |
| `bags/{slug}` (canon) | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | only while no working handle stands (the floor) | fleet | `grants.wikiUrl` = the catalog's `bags/{slug}` oracle | `bags/{slug}/` via the `selfCanon` grant |
| `libraryBags[]` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet | the recipe record's `bag-stack` minus `structuralSlots` (the lares bag is a library like the lararium bag), laid at boot and reconciled live (`recipe-watch.ts`) | `bags/lares/`, `bags/lararium/`, `bags/crossroads/` for the literal grants |
| `bags/oracle` (floor) | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet · federatable | `grants.islandUrl` | none |

Two facts the table hides. (1) ''Every CRDT slot registers `writable:true`'' — the island refuses nothing at the store; the cascade alone decides where a save lands. (2) ''A DELETE lands where the save landed.'' `island-adaptor.ts` keeps the LAST-KNOWN-SLOT map (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/config/slot-of`, a session `Map<title, SlotUri>`): fed at every outbound save with the cascade's verdict and at every inbound apply with the envelope's bag; `deleteTiddler` reads it before the cascade, falls back to the cascade's title read for a title never seen this session, and tombstones through `tombstoneInBag(slot, …)`. Witnesses: `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/routing-totality.test.ts` "a delete lands where the save landed" (+ the `$:/temp/*` CONTROL) and `tests/lar-kind.test.ts` (a draft's delete lands in the draft slot).''

!!! B. The daemon ISLAND composite (`recipe: { wikiSlug: "daemon" }`)

Same kernel (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-daemon-vm.ts`; browser `open-browser-vessel.ts`). The grants carry `islandUrl`, `wikiUrl` (= the daemon bag) and `catalogUrl` only, so at open `slotUrl` returns null for draft/working/personal and those slots ''prune for want of a handle''; `crossroads` splices in as a library (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-vm-core.ts`). Then — the daemon reads as a wiki (ruling) — its own behavior LATE-ATTACHES a working layer: `attachDaemonWorking` (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts`) resolves `wikis/daemon/working` through THE ONE slot-doc resolver under the same binding law as every wiki, splices it above the daemon bag `defaultWritable: true`, registers the slot URI with keyhive (delegated to a seated face), and re-seeds `current-wiki-bag` to it. The attach runs after the keyhive and the veil stand, inside the fail-closed boot window; a failed attach leaves the floor (the daemon bag), never a red.

| layer (top wins) | writable | default | sync class | disk mirror |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wikis/daemon/temp` | yes | never | device | none |
| `wikis/daemon/working` (late-attached) | yes | ''YES'' | fleet | none — `disk-projector` excludes `daemon` (owed) |
| `bags/daemon` (the daemon bag: verbs, outcomes, bindings — the control plane) | yes | only until the attach | fleet (private plane) | none — excluded by design |
| `bags/crossroads` | yes | no | fleet · federatable | `bags/crossroads/` on the wiki-island grant, none here |
| `bags/lares` · `bags/lararium` | yes | no | fleet | none here |
| `bags/oracle` | yes | no | fleet · federatable | none |

The two-vessel e2e witnesses the attach (`[daemon] working layer attached: lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/daemon/working`). A draft in the daemon wiki still routes to `wikis/daemon/draft` — a bag with NO layer — and `composite.put` refuses loud; the daemon gained `working` by ruling, not draft or personal.

!!! C. The HOST composite (VM-free, one per vessel)

`assembleVessel` + `mountWikiSlot` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/open-vessel-core.ts`), invoked by `wikiCap` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts`) — which now requires the daemon cap and awaits its `workerEa`, because the draft doc resolves through the daemon's slot-doc resolver (`resolveSlotDocs`, `vessel-steps.ts`) — the SAME call the island mount makes, so host and island mount ONE draft doc for one slug.

| layer (top wins) | writable | default | sync class | doc keyed by |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wikis/{slug}/temp` | yes | never | device | fresh `MemoryTiddlerStore` |
| `wikis/{slug}/draft` | yes | no | fleet when seated · device when not | THE ONE slot-doc resolver, by the daemon proxy |
| `bags/{slug}` | yes | ''yes'' — the host mounts no working layer, so the canon bag holds the floor | fleet | catalog `bags/{slug}` |
| PersonaGroup · circles · identities · sessions · `bags/daemon` | yes | yes (no `defaultWritable` given → true; registered BELOW the wiki, so the wiki's canon shadows them) | fleet (private) | bootstrap |
| `bags/lares` · `bags/lararium` | yes | no | fleet | oracle well-known tiddlers |
| `bags/oracle` | yes | no | fleet · federatable | genesis |
| `bags/catalog` | ''no'' | — | fleet (private) | catalog-url file |

The host mounts NO `working` and NO `personal` layer. A role cap composed alongside the core (the meshpalace FLOW-map layer, `defaultWritable: true`) may register AFTER the wiki cap in topo order and take the host composite's office — unmeasured; nothing writes bagless through the host composite today.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/as-routed>>

!! The cascade ~ which KIND of tiddler lands where today

The in-wiki cascade `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/config/bag-paths` (`packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/lar-bag-paths.tid:5-18`) walks newline-separated filters against the saving title; first non-empty result names the slot, an empty operand from a NAMED rule withholds, and no match names a router gap that still lands at `current-wiki-bag` with a console warning (`island-adaptor.ts:118-160`). Every rule reads the ''title''; no rule reads a field (`island-adaptor.ts:284-289` states why: a delete runs after the tiddler has gone).

| kind of raw tiddler | rule (`lar-bag-paths.tid`) | lands in | sync |
|---|---|---|---|
| `$:/core`, `$:/library/sjcl.js` | `:5-6` withhold | nowhere (engine bytes ride CAS) | — |
| `$:/temp/*`, `$:/status/*`, `$:/boot/*`, `$:/HistoryList*` | `:7-10` | `wikis/{slug}/temp` | device |
| `$:/StoryList*`, `$:/state/folded/*`, `$:/state/tab-*`, `$:/palette*` — the set `lar-kind[]` names `personal` (`filters/lar-kind.ts`, ONE spelling; the cascade reads `[lar-kind[]match[personal]…]`) | `:11` | `wikis/{slug}/personal` | fleet |
| every other `$:/state/*` | `:15` | `wikis/{slug}/temp` | device |
| a tiddler whose `draft.of` FIELD stands (`[is[draft]…]`, TW5's own predicate) | `:13` | `wikis/{slug}/draft` | fleet |
| `lar:*` | `:17` | `current-wiki-bag` = `wikis/{slug}/working` (daemon: `bags/daemon`) | fleet |
| anything else, including a foreign-titled pack member (`HelloThere`) and every other `$:/` system tiddler | `:18` catch-all | `current-wiki-bag` | fleet |

''The `draft.of` FIELD is the switch'' (operator ruling 2026-09-11, quote license: "Approve moving to `draft.of` as the switch (pono w/ TW5 server/client setups)"). TW5 decides draft-ness by that field (`TiddlyWiki5/core/modules/tiddler.js:20-22`) and mints the title through a LOCALIZED language string — `Draft/Title`, or `Draft/Attribution` when `$:/status/UserName` stands, yielding `Draft of 'X' by <user>` (`TiddlyWiki5/core/modules/wiki.js:1725-1735`) — so the title decides nothing: the cascade's draft rule reads `[is[draft]…]` and `lar-kind[]` reads `Tiddler.isDraft`, on a stock server and an island alike (`tests/lar-kind.test.ts`; the live-server witness in `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts`). The ruling's spelling `draft-of` (hyphen) names no TW5 field; TW5 spells it `draft.of`. ''The delete path:'' a delete runs after the tiddler has gone, so the field cannot be read then — the adaptor owes a LAST-KNOWN-SLOT map (fed at every outbound save with the cascade's verdict and at every inbound apply with the envelope's `$origin-bag`; read by `deleteTiddler` before the cascade; a title never seen this session falls back to the cascade's title read). The red stands in `tests/lar-kind.test.ts` until `island-adaptor.ts` lands it.

''What the nalu stamps.'' Every inbound record gains `$origin-bag` from the ENVELOPE (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/modules/nalu-engine.ts:112-116`); the projector routes a flush by that stamp (`packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector.ts:280-283`), and the outbound save strips it before the put (`island-adaptor.ts:352-355`). No persisted field names a bag.

!!! Verb seats

| seat | resolves the bag how | lands in | file:line |
|---|---|---|---|
| in-wiki edit / save | the cascade, by kind — `IslandAdaptor.saveTiddler` | per the table above | `island-adaptor.ts` `saveTiddler` / `_writeMeme` — ⚠ MEASURED: nothing in the tree carries a LIVE wiki change out to `saveTiddler`/`deleteTiddler` (only `wiki-sync` sessions and tests call them; `$tw.syncer` does not run). The seat is right; the outbound bridge is OWED |
| in-wiki delete | the last-known-slot map, else the cascade's title read → `tombstoneInBag` | the bag the save landed in | `island-adaptor.ts` `deleteTiddler` |
| `meme put` (no target) | the daemon's own `$tw.wiki` → its cascade → `current-wiki-bag` | `wikis/daemon/working` once the late-attach re-seeds the cascade (the daemon bag until then) — and stands in `$tw.wiki` alone until the outbound bridge lands (the row above) | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts` `anchorBagOf` |
| `meme put --recipe <slug>` | THE PUT LAW: the recipe RECORD's `writable-bag` = `wikis/<slug>/working`, else the top of its `bag-stack` (`designatedBagOf`, `@lararium/mesh` recipe.ts) → a mounted writable layer of the DAEMON island, else the instance slot's doc through THE ONE slot-doc resolver, else reach by catalog | the SAME working doc the wiki island mounts — the placement surfaces in the running wiki (two-vessel e2e ⑤ ★) | `meme-verbs.ts` `reachRecipeBag` / `storeOfBag` |
| `meme get --recipe <slug>` | THE GET LAW: the whole cascade top-down (`expandRecipe(recipeFromRecord(rec))`), the first bag holding the meme LIVE; the designated bag's store when none does (a null read, never a refusal) | the stack — draft shadows canon; canon answers through `--recipe` when the drafts hold nothing | `meme-verbs.ts` `reachRecipeBag`; `tests/meme-verbs.test.ts` "READS THE STACK" |
| `meme put --bag <slug>` | `compositeMemeSink` → `composite.put({bag})` on the daemon island | that bag's writable layer, else refuses (no shadow-up) | `meme-verbs.ts:177-179`, `composite-store.ts:218-244` |
| `act ADD / COPY / MOVE / LOAD / INGEST --to <bag>` | `BagAccess`: a mounted writable layer, else the catalog/oracle accessor's own store (write-then-sync) | the named bag exactly | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/action-handler.ts:243-270`, `:1170-1186` |
| `lares ingest --source <dir> --to <bag>` | the caller names `--to`; a `wikis/` source only changes the URI derivation | the named bag | `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/ingest.ts:27-33`, `packages/lares-cli/src/ingest-core.ts:118-131` |
| `draft` verb (`makeDraftReactor`) | `toBag` else `defaultWritableBagId()` | the daemon's working layer by default | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/wiki-draft-handlers.ts` |
| `where` / `wiki which` | the mounted composite, every registered bag by access, AND every registered wiki's instance slots through THE ONE resolver (a floor doc answers under its slot name, never its registry key) | membership | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/worker-data-verbs.ts` `makeWhereReactor` |
| recipe-watch library mount | `bag-stack` minus `structuralSlots(slug)` | inserted above `bags/lares`, `writable:true, defaultWritable:false` | `recipe-watch.ts` |

''The recipe record and the mount struct spell ONE shape.'' `recipeRecordFields(recipe)` (`@lararium/mesh` wiki-recipe.ts) writes `bag-stack` = the expanded cascade bottom-up minus the four instance slots (the oracle floor, the libraries, the wiki's own canon) and `writable-bag` = `wikis/{slug}/working`; `recipeFromRecord(rec, slug)` reads it back; both minters call it (`genesis-doc.ts` `systemRecipe`; `wiki-mint-handlers.ts` init). The catalog registry never rides a bag-stack (access ≠ load). `CompositeStore.getRecipe` / `putViaRecipe` / `buildLayersFromRecipe` and the camelCase `RecipeTiddler` are retired. Witness: `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/recipe-record.test.ts`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/as-written>>

!! What the canon carriers say, and where they contradict the code or each other

| carrier | says | the code | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| `wiki-layer-ontology#/write-law` (`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology.mem:181`) | "a draft/volatile tiddler → `@temp`" | `Draft of ` routes to the CRDT `draft` slot (`lar-bag-paths.tid:16`) | contradicted the code AND the ruling — HEALED by the aftermath spiral (the law now reads `@draft` for drafts, `@temp` for volatile) |
| `wiki-layer-ontology#/naming-law` | instance mounts "MUST NOT enter `@catalog`" | the draft FLOOR doc (`wikis/{slug}/drafts/{DID}`) registers in the catalog; a face binding never does | RE-TRUED — the law now carves the floor out: a per-DID device doc is a registry entry the vessel holds by access, not an instance MOUNT of a group |
