| `save-path` SP-4 (`:96-99`) | "If `fields["bag"]` carries an explicit bag URI, `saveTiddler` MUST use it" | "no field names a bag" (`island-adaptor.ts:254`); `bag` rides as the author's field, ignored for routing | contradicted the code — HEALED (SP-4 now states the envelope law) |
| `disk-projection#/bag-roles` (`bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection.mem:54-60`) | `@draft` "none — runtime", `@personal` "none — mesh-synced", `@working` → `wikis/{slug}/`, canon → `bags/` | matches the grants (`open-node-vessel.ts:1631-1656`) | agrees |
| `disk-projection#/projection-routing` rule 2 (`:141`) | "Every other tiddler follows the standard TW5 path … One tiddler, one file" | `carrierBaseRelPath` returns null for any non-`lar:///w.w.w/` title (`packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts:84-99`); a foreign-titled `.tid` never reaches disk; a pack rides `OriginalTiddlerPaths` + REPACK instead | contradicted the code for foreign titles — HEALED (rule 2 now names the siting requirement + REPACK) |
| `disk-projection#/projection-routing` rule 3 (`:142`) | siting overrides ride `config/disk-paths` and `config/disk-extensions` | `makeTw5FileInfo` accepts `pathFilters`/`extFilters` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-file-info.ts:46-48`) and `exportCarrierFile` passes neither (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-write.ts:57`, `:76`); the only mention sits in a comment (`bag-paths.ts:30`) | designed, unwired — MARKED OWED on the carrier |
| `bag-wiki-uri-split#/live-vs-canon` (`bag-wiki-uri-split.mem`) | `wikis/{slug}` = the live wiki; the `@working`/`@draft`/`@personal` binding per (PersonaGroup × fingerprint) | host and island read ONE resolver; the draft floor stands when no seat does | agrees |
| `residency-model#/tai-chi` (`residency-model.mem:208-211`) | temp among the coordinates "keyed by (PersonaGroup × recipe-fingerprint)" | temp holds no key; a fresh `MemoryTiddlerStore` per boot (`island-recipe.ts:67-70`) | overstated — HEALED (temp drawn outside the keyed set) |
| `wiki-layer-ontology#/the-daemon-wiki` | the daemon's write layer falls back to its own bag; a late-attach working layer owed | the late attach STANDS (`attachDaemonWorking`); the disk mirror for `daemon` remains excluded | agrees; the attach is built, the mirror owed |
