<<~ ahu #/the-blur>>

!! The blur, named

# ''`writable-bag` vs the mount's default'' — DISSOLVED. The record designates `wikis/{slug}/working`; the mount's ONE default writable is the working slot (`slotLayerFlags`), the canon bag only while no working handle stands; temp never. Three writers, one answer: the working layer.
# ''Two draft documents wear one slot name'' — DISSOLVED. THE ONE slot-doc resolver (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/slot-doc-resolver.ts`, the law `resolveSlotDoc` in `@lararium/mesh`): the PersonaGroup × fingerprint binding WHEN the vessel holds a seated PersonaGroup cap, ELSE the device floor `wikis/{slug}/drafts/{did}` — and the record says which (`face-reach`). Every site reads through it: the island's slot grants, the host mount (by the daemon proxy), `wiki init`, `prune-stale`, `meme put --recipe`, `where`, the ACTION verbs. Weld witness: `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/slot-doc-resolver.test.ts` S3 (five sites, one doc, seated and unseated). ⚠ THE MOUNT'S TRACE IS THE TRACE: a wiki the vessel mounted this session fingerprinted the canon doc it holds; a verb re-deriving the url from a registry pointer read a DIFFERENT doc when a peer's founding rewrote the shared oracle plane's `bags/lares` pointer mid-session (measured in the two-vessel e2e) — the resolver keeps the mount's trace per slug and reuses it.
# ''Per-DID or per-PersonaGroup'' — RULED: both, by seat. Fleet when a PersonaGroup sync-fleet cap stands; the DID floor when not — a private device so far. A seat landing later resolves the face doc from then on; the floor stays the device's own (no migration).
# ''What "volatile / per-device" holds today: temp ALONE.'' Presence stands unbuilt — no `presence` slot, no `$:/status/` beyond what TW5 writes; `$:/status/*` and `$:/boot/*` and most `$:/state/*` route to temp (`lar-bag-paths.tid:8-10`, `:15`). `personal` fleet-syncs by design (view state), so the ruling's "all here don't [sync]" holds for temp and not for personal. Per-device state that MUST survive a reboot (a device's own window layout, a local-only bag pin) has no home: temp forgets at boot, personal follows the fleet.
# ''A draft routes by its `draft.of` FIELD on SAVE; the DELETE owes a last-known-slot map.'' RULED 2026-09-11 (the field is the switch). The cascade's `[is[draft]…]` reads the tiddler the save carries; a delete runs after the tiddler has gone (`island-adaptor.ts:284-289`), so the adaptor records the slot each title last routed to (outbound: the cascade verdict; inbound: the envelope's `$origin-bag`) and tombstones there, falling back to the cascade's title read for a title never seen this session. Owed to `island-adaptor.ts`; the red stands in `tests/lar-kind.test.ts`.
# ''A non-meme file enters by three doors and leaves by one, and foreign titles leave by none.'' Enter: (a) `lares ingest --source --to` scans `.mem` and any extension, pairs a `.meta` sidecar, derives the URI by the loci law (`ingest-core.ts:83-88`, `:111-113`, `:171-181`); the island runs `tw5.parseFields(meta)` then `tw5.deserialize(ext, text, base)` (`action-handler.ts:863-873`) and packs foreign-titled members into `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` (`:815-833`). (b) `act LOAD --to` takes carriers with the verb, same registry route (`:641-707`). (c) the in-wiki drag-drop / `$:/Import` ride TW5's own DOM deserializer and then the cascade — no house code touches it. Leave: the ONE render shore `exportCarrierFile` (`meme-write.ts:40-77`) → `makeTw5FileInfo` (`tw5-file-info.ts:88-176`) picks `.tid` / content + `.meta` / `.json` exactly as `generateTiddlerFileInfo` does, base64 for a binary type (`:140`), and the projector sites it at `<uri-path><ext>` (`disk-projector.ts:352-360`). But `carrierBaseRelPath` sites only `lar:///w.w.w/…` names (`bag-paths.ts:84-99`): a `.png` ingested under a loci URI round-trips; a `HelloThere.tid` pack member reaches disk only through REPACK of its pack (`action-handler.ts:352-370`).
# ''`meme get --recipe` reads the designated bag, not the stack'' — DISSOLVED by ruling ("The stack."). GET walks the whole cascade top-down and answers from the first bag holding the meme live; PUT writes the designated bag alone. Witness: `tests/meme-verbs.test.ts` "READS THE STACK"; two-vessel e2e ⑦ ★ (canon answers through `--recipe` on B).
# ''Two recipe shapes, one name'' — DISSOLVED. `recipeRecordFields` ⇆ `recipeFromRecord` (`@lararium/mesh` wiki-recipe.ts); `catalog` leaves the user stack; the lares bag is a library like the lararium bag (a record that names it mounts it). The libraries a record names lay at boot AND reconcile live.
# ''`working` and `personal` against the four strata'' — RULED. "named wiki bag" = `working` (the disk sentence decides it; the shore-law MOVE stays the promotion door); `personal` keeps its own layer while the browser UX stands up. The daemon reads as a wiki and holds `working` too (late-attached).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/one-model>>

!! One model ~ the fewest changes that satisfy the ruling

''The layer list per recipe'' (bottom → top), reading the ruling's four strata onto the slots that already exist:

| ruling stratum | slot | store | sync | disk | writable | default |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| canon bags | `bags/oracle` · `libraryBags[]` · `bags/{slug}` | CRDT | fleet (+ federatable where the plane allows) | `bags/{name}/` on ingest and on promotion MOVE | by ACTION verb only | no |
| named wiki bag | `wikis/{slug}/working` | CRDT | fleet | `wikis/{slug}/` | the cascade's catch-all | ''YES — the ONE default'' |
| drafts | `wikis/{slug}/draft` (absorbs `personal` as a KIND, see below) | CRDT | fleet | none | the cascade's draft rule | no |
| volatile | `wikis/{slug}/temp` | memory | device | none | the cascade's temp rules | no |

''What stands'' (each red-first, each witnessed): the default writable moved to `working` (mesh `slotLayerFlags`; witnesses in `composite-store.test.ts`); the delete routes like the save through the last-known-slot map (`routing-totality.test.ts`, `lar-kind.test.ts`); ONE slot-doc resolver, floor-falling (`slot-doc-resolver.test.ts`); `meme get --recipe` reads the stack, `meme put --recipe` writes the designated bag (`meme-verbs.test.ts`); the recipe record and the mount struct converge (`recipe-record.test.ts`); the daemon holds a late-attached `working` layer (two-vessel e2e); `wiki init` registers `wikis/{slug}/working` and the vessel's `registerBags` carries it, so the cap gate knows the working slot; the `.meta` sidecar merges OVER the deserialized record as TW5's loader rules (`action-handler.ts`, both doors).

''What remains'' (owed, named):

* ''The outbound bridge.'' No live wiki change reaches `IslandAdaptor.saveTiddler` / `deleteTiddler` on any island — only `wiki-sync` sessions and tests call them, and `$tw.syncer` does not run. In-wiki edits and the anchor `meme put` stand in `$tw.wiki` alone. The cascade, the map and the seats are right; the wire from the wiki's change event to the adaptor is the act missing.
* ''The daemon's disk mirror.'' `disk-projector` excludes `daemon`; `wikis/daemon/working` reaches no disk.
* ''The shared oracle plane moves.'' A joiner's founding rewrote the founder's oracle-plane `bags/lares` pointer (measured: `automerge:ZqADt…` mounted, `automerge:2St9f…` after B stood). A reboot of A would mount B's lares doc. Not this carrier's to rule; named.
* ''Disk legs for non-meme files:'' the siting cascades ride (#/tw5-surfaces); binaries under `bags/` read OPEN (talk-story).
* ''The host composite's office.'' A role cap's `defaultWritable: true` layer (meshpalace) may register after the wiki cap; nothing writes bagless through the host composite today.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/questions>>

!! Questions the operator answered, and the one still open

# ''Does a draft fleet-sync, or stay on the device?'' RULED: fleet when a PersonaGroup sync-fleet cap stands, else the device floor; the cap-stack falls to the floor, never reds.
# ''Does `personal` survive as a layer?'' RULED: its own layer, while the browser UX stands up.
# ''Which per-device state MUST survive a reboot?'' OPEN. Temp forgets; personal follows the fleet; the draft floor of an unseated vessel is the one per-device CRDT doc today.
# ''Does "named wiki bag" mean `working`?'' RULED by the disk sentence: `working`; the shore-law MOVE stays the promotion door.
# ''Does `meme get --recipe` read the stack?'' RULED: "The stack."
# ''Does the `draft.of` FIELD decide routing?'' RULED: the field is the switch; the delete rides the last-known-slot map.
# ''Which non-meme file types enter through `lares ingest`?'' Every extension, through TW5's registry; binaries under `bags/` read OPEN (talk-story).
# ''Does the daemon wiki gain its `working` layer?'' RULED: working layers for all wikis; the late attach stands.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/tw5-surfaces>>

!! TW5 surfaces for non-meme workflows ~ what exists, what the house rides

| surface | where (fork) | does | the house |
|---|---|---|---|
| `$tw.utils.registerFileType` · `$tw.config.contentTypeInfo` · `fileExtensionInfo` · `getFileExtensionInfo` · `getTypeEncoding` | `TiddlyWiki5/boot/boot.js:553-583` | the ONE registry: content-type ↔ extension ↔ encoding ↔ `deserializerType` | rides (`tw5-file-info.ts:135-140`, `action-handler.ts:110-135`) |
| `$tw.wiki.deserializeTiddlers(type, text, srcFields)` | `boot.js:1641-1670` | routes by deserializer name, content type, extension, `deserializerType`, then `text/plain` | rides (`action-handler.ts:127-128`) |
| boot deserializers `tid` · `tids` (multids) · `txt` · `html` · `json` · `js` · `css` · `dom` | `boot.js:1687-1835`; `core/modules/deserializers.js` | the packs (`.json` array, `.multids`, `.html` store-area) | rides through the registry; pack membership aside in `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` (`action-handler.ts:815-833`) |
| `$tw.utils.parseFields` | `boot.js:428` | `.meta` and `.tid` header parsing | rides (`action-handler.ts:129-132`) |
| `$tw.loadTiddlersFromFile` · `$tw.loadMetadataForFile` · `$tw.loadTiddlersFromPath` · `$tw.loadTiddlersFromSpecification` (`tiddlywiki.files`) · `$tw.loadPluginFolder` · `$tw.loadWikiTiddlers` | `boot.js:1941-1964`, `:1969-1976`, `:1988-2013`, `:2017`, `:2168`, `:2293` | node-only disk walkers; `.meta` sidecar merged onto the first tiddler; `maxEditFileSize` guard; `excludeRegExp` skips `*.meta` (`:1983`) | ''does not ride'' — the house walks disk in `ingest-core.ts` (`git ls-files`-shaped, declaration-read) and hands bytes to the registry; `tiddlywiki.files` specifications and `plugin.info` folders stay unread |
| `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` | `boot.js:2369` | the file-path ↔ title map the folder loader keeps | rides the same title for pack provenance (`action-handler.ts:833`) |
| `generateTiddlerFileInfo` · `generateTiddlerFilepath` · `saveTiddlerToFile(Sync)` · `deleteTiddlerFile` · `cleanupTiddlerFiles` | `TiddlyWiki5/core-server/filesystem.js:213`, `:322`, `:445`, `:487`, `:508`, `:549` | type selection (.tid / content+.meta / .json), path sanitizing, the write | ''re-implemented pure'' in `tw5-file-info.ts:88-176` (no `fs`); the projector writes (`disk-projector.ts:352-400`) |
| `$:/config/FileSystemPaths` · `$:/config/FileSystemExtensions` | `plugins/tiddlywiki/filesystem/filesystemadaptor.js:59-65` | the siting and extension cascades | ''rides, one spelling'' — `exportCarrierFile` reads the two `$:/` tiddlers EXACTLY as the adaptor does (a REAL tiddler, `tiddlerExists`; `tw5-file-info.ts` `readSitingCascades`) and the projector sites a ruled path first, the loci law otherwise (`disk-projector.ts` `flush`, the `sited` memory = `$tw.boot.files`); no `lar:` twin — a spelling honoured by one door only is the disagreement. Parity against the fork's own `generateTiddlerFileInfo`: `tests/tw5-file-info-parity.test.ts` |
| the `filesystem` syncadaptor · `syncer.js` · `$:/config/SyncFilter` | `filesystemadaptor.js:86`; `core/modules/syncer.js:19`, `:67`; `core/wiki/config/SyncFilter.tid` | TW5's own save-to-disk loop and its total-minus-exclusions filter | ''does not ride'' the adaptor; the cascade takes SyncFilter's SHAPE (`island-adaptor.ts:107-111`) |
| `isSystemTiddler` · `isTemporaryTiddler` · `isVolatileTiddler` · `Tiddler.isDraft` · `generateDraftTitle` | `core/modules/wiki.js:222-232`, `:1725`; `core/modules/tiddler.js:20-22` | the kind predicates TW5 itself uses (`$:/` · `$:/temp/` · `$:/temp/volatile/` · the `draft.of` field · the localized draft title) | ''rides'' — `[lar-kind[]]` (`filters/lar-kind.ts`) answers `volatile` · `temporary` · `draft` · `personal` · `system` · `content` by calling these predicates plus the house's personal set; the cascade routes drafts by `[is[draft]…]` and personal by `[lar-kind[]match[personal]…]` (`lar-bag-paths.tid:11`, `:13`) |
| `--load` · `--save` · `--savetiddlers` · `--savewikifolder` · `--render` · `--import` · `--unpackplugin` | `TiddlyWiki5/core-server/commands/` | the CLI legs for a folder wiki | `--render`'s law rides in `meme-project.ts:104`; the rest stay stubs the house never calls |
| `$:/Import` · dropzone · `th-importing-tiddler` | `core/modules/widgets/` (dropzone, navigator) | in-browser file drop → DOM deserializer → the wiki | rides untouched; a dropped file then saves through the cascade like any edit |
| MWS (multi-wiki server) | absent from this fork (`plugins/tiddlywiki/` holds `filesystem` and `tiddlyweb` only) | — | nothing to ride |

''Reading.'' The house stands on the registry and the deserializer chain, re-implements the filesystem module's pure half (parity-witnessed against the fork's own module), reads the siting cascades as the adaptor reads them, and answers the kind of a raw tiddler by TW5's own predicates. What it lacks names itself: the disk walker's `tiddlywiki.files` and plugin-folder legs (never needed while `ingest` reads declarations).

''The non-meme round trip, measured'' (`tests/e2e/nonmeme-parity.test.ts`, both doors real): `note.md` + `.meta` — bytes identical, fields identical; `pack.json` — both doors keep the membership in `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` (the server only under `retain-original-tiddler-path`), and the server's `--savewikifolder` explodes the pack into per-member `.tid` files where the island keeps it packed (REPACK) — named, on purpose. Two strays: (1) the island seeds the `.meta` BEFORE the deserialize (`action-handler.ts:870-873`) where TW5 merges it AFTER (`boot.js:1961`), so `type: text/markdown` in a sidecar lands as `text/x-markdown` on the island — a red held in the witness, owed to `action-handler.ts`; (2) `$origin-bag` reached the sidecar — cured in `tw5-file-info.ts` (`UNPERSISTED_FIELDS`). MEASURED, OPEN: a `.png` under bags/ enters the island as a skinny handle `photo.tid` on the `cid/` tier and the `.png` sweeps; the server keeps `photo.png` + `.meta` whole.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/aftermath>>

!! Aftermath ~ the blast-radius spiral (operator-approved)

The spiral walked every carrier the #/as-written table names and evergreened the ones whose text described retired code: `wiki-layer-ontology#/write-law` (drafts → `@draft`, volatile → `@temp`, title-read), `save-path` SP-3/SP-4 (the cascade rule; the envelope law, no `bag` field routes), `disk-projection#/projection-routing` (the siting requirement for rule 2; rule 3 marked OWED), `residency-model#/tai-chi` (temp outside the keyed set), `bag-wiki-uri-split` meta (`standing`, half-enactment named). The `lares-history` tree stays untouched (history, never canon).

''Tensions the first spiral surfaced, and how they closed:'' `wiki-layer-ontology#/naming-law` — re-trued to carve the draft FLOOR out (a per-DID device doc, a registry entry, never an instance mount of a group); `personal-slot#/scoping-mechanism` — the seat decides (binding when seated, floor when not); the four strata against five slots — ruled (`working` is the named wiki bag, `personal` stays); the `draft.of` field — ruled (the switch, with the delete map); the default writable = temp — cured red-first. What remains stands under #/one-model "What remains".

<<~/ahu>>

